1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,740
ANGELA: Hello, Flanders conference hotel.

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:10,600
MAN: Oh, hi. I wanted to ask about conference facilities at the hotel.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,590
Have I come through to the right person?

4
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:16,960
ANGELA: You have. I'm the customer services manager

5
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:22,090
My name's Angela. So how can I help you?

6
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:25,280
MAN: Well, I'm calling from Barrett and Stansons

7
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,430
we're a medical company based in Perth.

8
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:30,470
ANGELA: Oh yes.

9
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:35,730
MAN: And we're organising a conference for our clients to be held in Sydney.

10
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:40,990
It'll be held over two days and we're expecting about fifty or sixty people.

11
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:44,080
ANGELA: When were you thinking of having it?

12
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:51,110
MAN: Some time early next year, like the end of January? It'd have to be a weekend.

13
00:00:51,110 --> 00:01:00,330
ANGELA: Let me see... our conference facilities are already booked for the weekend beginning January 28th.

14
00:01:00,330 --> 00:01:04,940
We could do the first weekend in February?

15
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:08,820
MAN: How about January 21st?

16
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:13,730
ANGELA: I'm afraid that's booked too.

17
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:17,830
MAN: Well, let's go for the February date then.

18
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:22,580
ANGELA: So that's the weekend beginning the 4th.

19
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:29,670
MAN: OK. Now can you tell me a bit about what conference facilities you have?

20
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:36,890
ANGELA: Sure. So for talks and presentations we have the Tesla room.

21
00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:38,640
MAN: Sorry?

22
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,808
ANGELA: Tesla - that's spelled T-E-S-L-A.

23
00:01:41,808 --> 00:01:52,580
It holds up to a hundred people, and it's fully equipped with a projector and so on.

24
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,280
MAN: How about a microphone?

25
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:59,095
ANGELA: Yes, that'll be all set up ready for you,

26
00:01:59,095 --> 00:02:05,200
and there'll be one that members of the audience can use too, for questions, if necessary.

27
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:10,060
MAN: Fine. And we'll also need some sort of open area

28
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:12,755
where people can sit and have a cup of coffee,

29
00:02:12,755 --> 00:02:18,152
and we'd like to have an exhibition of our products and services there as well,

30
00:02:18,152 --> 00:02:21,390
so that'll need to be quite a big space.

31
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:26,332
ANGELA: That's fine, there's a central atrium with all those facilities,

32
00:02:26,332 --> 00:02:33,070
and you can come before the conference starts if you want to set everything up.

33
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:37,420
MAN: Great. And I presume there's wifi?

34
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:43,420
ANGELA: Oh, yes, that's free and available throughout the hotel.

35
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,520
MAN: OK.

36
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:49,643
ANGELA: Would you also like us to provide a buffet lunch?

37
00:02:49,643 --> 00:02:54,140
We can do a two-course meal with a number of different options.

38
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:58,010
MAN: What sort of price are we looking at for that?

39
00:02:58,010 --> 00:03:04,106
ANGELA: Well, I can send you a copy of the standard menu.

40
00:03:04,106 --> 00:03:10,710
That's $45 per person. Or you can have the special for $25 more.

41
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:16,299
MAN: I think the standard should be ok, but yes, send me the menu.

42
00:03:16,299 --> 00:03:23,085
MAN: Now we're also going to need accommodation on the Saturday night for some of the participants...

43
00:03:23,085 --> 00:03:26,678
I'm not sure how many, but probably about 25.

44
00:03:26,678 --> 00:03:29,770
So what do you charge for a room?

45
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:35,760
ANGELA: Well, for conference attendees we have a 25% reduction

46
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:41,744
so we can offer you rooms at $135.

47
00:03:41,744 --> 00:03:45,070
Normally a standard room's $180.

48
00:03:45,070 --> 00:03:48,120
MAN: And does that include breakfast?

49
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:54,925
ANGELA: Sure. And of course, guests can also make use of all the other facilities at the hotel.

50
00:03:54,925 --> 00:04:00,595
So we've got a spa where you can get massages and facials and so on,

51
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:05,510
and there's a pool up on the roof for the use of guests.

52
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:13,210
MAN: Great. Now what about transport links? The hotel's downtown, isn't it?

53
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:17,520
ANGELA: Yes, it's about 12 kilometres from the airport

54
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:20,719
but there's a complimentary shuttle bus for guests.

55
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:26,020
And it's only about ten minutes' walk from the central railway station.

56
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:30,240
MAN: OK. Now, I don't know Sydney very well

57
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:34,130
can you just give me an idea of the location of the hotel?

58
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:38,960
ANGELA: Well, it's downtown on Wilby Street

59
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,807
that's quite a small street, and it's not very far from the sea.

60
00:04:41,807 --> 00:04:50,635
And of course if the conference attendees want to go out on the Saturday evening there's a huge choice of places to eat.

61
00:04:50,635 --> 00:04:54,473
Then if they want to make a night of it,

62
00:04:54,473 --> 00:04:58,660
they can go on to one of the clubs in the area

63
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:02,150
there are a great many to choose from.

64
00:05:02,150 --> 00:05:07,000
MAN: OK. So if we go ahead with this

65
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,500
can you give me some information about how much...
